model g11_settle_order
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T, tally 2.1.2 (issue #44), G11: L §5.14.3 How a settlement leg counts, E §5 step 5, E §3.2: turn swaps t[2026-03]'s places, so bank[r1], settling its adjustment, is refused (RUN-RECORD, the leg is turned round), and linking is all or nothing: every read that counts the adjustment meets that refusal, in either order, two reads in one ask (q_fb: flows then a balance; q_bf: the balance then flows; q_ff: flows twice). The twin g11/settle_order_twin moves only the leg's from place, and its row settles: both orders answer the same numbers. tally 2.1.1's refcore linked the adjustment before the refusal, so the later read of an ask took the HOLE-CHANGED hole, and swapping the reads swapped the answers."

source plan "T's invented plan"

source act "T's invented act"

source bank_feed "T's invented bank feed"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place konto2: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

input amt: money PLN

input dom: int

input src: key accounts

input dst: key accounts

input bank: observed

def s_[m in months]: key accounts = src at start_of(m)

def d_[m in months]: key accounts = dst at start_of(m)

move t[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from s_[m] to d_[m] amount amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN
  dom = 10
  src = konto
  dst = konto2
  opening[konto] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version turn
  cite act
  governs 2026-03
  known 2026-05-01
  replace src = konto2
  replace dst = konto

version settle
  cite bank_feed
  governs 2026-05
  known 2026-05-20
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-05-15, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto2 to konto amount 100.00 PLN, fulfils: adjustments[t[2026-03].cash, turn]) "line 1"

ask q_fb: flows(t, 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-31), bal(konto, 2026-06-30)

ask q_bf: bal(konto, 2026-06-30), flows(t, 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-31)

ask q_ff: flows(t, 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-31), flows(t, 2026-05-01 .. 2026-05-31)

ask zm1: explain t[2026-01]

ask zm2: explain t[2026-02]

ask zm3: explain t[2026-03]

ask zm4: explain t[2026-04]
